.\" elebake.8 - manual page (mdoc)
.Dd August 29, 2026
.Dt ELEBAKE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm elebake
.Nd compiler for a verified-boot trust chain (build, sign, deploy, attest)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
maintains the trust chain of a locally built FreeBSD boot loader:
checked-out source, measured expectations, Authenticode signature,
OpenPGP-attested manifest, deployment to removable boot media, and
tamper witnesses read back at boot.
.Pp
Every
.Nm
command is a
.Em generator :
it emits shell text describing an action.
Whether that text is displayed, piped, or executed is decided by an
.Em interpreter
the operator controls per function
.Pq see Sx ENVIRONMENT .
The shipped default displays
.Pq Ql cat :
inspect first, then pin an executing interpreter.
Batch commands emit an unconditional sequence of further
.Nm
commands; checking is itself a command in the sequence, and the batch
machinery stops at the first failure.
.Sh COMMANDS
The authoritative, always current command reference is built into the
tool:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
elebake help              # grouped command overview
elebake help <command>    # one command, parameters, examples
elebake help env [<VAR>]   # documented environment variables
elebake help intp <fn>     # interpreter resolution for a function
.Ed
.Pp
The command families, briefly:
.Bl -tag -width "environment"
.It Cm bootstrap , init , environment
Create a database
.Pq Cm bootstrap Ar name profile ,
install a variable profile
.Pq Cm environment init ,
manage the layered variable store
.Pq Cm setenv , getenv , unsetenv , printenv
and the environment cache.
.It Cm pem , openpgp , pkcs11
Key backends.
Records hold paths and URIs only
.Pq material stays where it lives ;
.Cm add
registers,
.Cm dump
emits the replay,
.Cm import
reproduces one extra record file,
.Cm prerequisites
checks the toolchain functionally.
.It Cm stage
The staging object: a named workspace for one boot tree.
.Cm add , checkout , build , install , include , sign , make
form the build pipeline;
.Cm sign-key , attest-key , filter , device , boot tree
bind records;
.Cm manifest , attest , verify , tree sync , deploy , push
publish to a medium;
.Cm marker , site mk , trust anchor , trust mk
provision the measured expectations;
.Cm dump , import , check stage
migrate whole stages between databases;
.Cm status , list
derive state from the artifacts.
.It Cm dump , restore , batch
Whole-database export as a replayable script
.Pq Sx FILES ,
and its replay.
The dump describes everything that is stored; the restore replays it
idempotently
.Pq keep-going ,
build artifacts are regenerated, never moved.
.It Cm help , help env , help intp , last , log , error
Documentation, trace inspection
.Pq Cm last
and logging.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
All configuration lives in
.Ev ELEBAKE_*
variables, layered as
.Pa .env/local
.Pq override ,
.Pa .env/default
.Pq installed profile
and shipped templates.
Key variables:
.Bl -tag -width "ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_<fn>"
.It Ev ELEBAKE_BASE
The active database
.Pq default Pa ~/.elebake/db .
.It Ev ELEBAKE_TERMINAL_INTERPRETER
What runs the emitted shell of terminals; default
.Ql cat
.Pq display .
Pin
.Ql sh
to execute.
.It Ev ELEBAKE_INTERPRETER_<fn>
Per-function override, arity-specific
.Pq Ql ..._stage_import4
before arity-agnostic.
An agnostic pin covers the whole family and is only legal when the
family is homogeneous.
.It Ev ELEBAKE_FREEBSD_SRC , ELEBAKE_STAND_BUILD_SUBDIRS
Source repository and the curated stand/ component lists for the build.
.El
.Pp
Every variable is documented in place:
.Ql elebake help env <VAR> .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "~/.elebake/current/.log/" -compact
.It Pa ~/.elebake/db
active database
.Pq symlink
.It Pa ~/.elebake/current/.log/
per-invocation traces - the debugging ground truth
.It Pa ~/.elebake/worktree/
git worktrees of the FreeBSD source; build trees live outside the
database
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Create a database, register keys, build and publish a stage:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
\&./elebake.sh bootstrap current minimal | sh
\&./elebake.sh pkcs11 add db 'pkcs11:token=...;object=db' /root/sb/db.crt
\&./elebake.sh openpgp add manifest 0123456789ABCDEF /root/sb/.gnupg
\&./elebake.sh stage add smoke1
\&./elebake.sh stage sign key smoke1 pkcs11 db
\&./elebake.sh stage attest key smoke1 openpgp manifest
\&./elebake.sh stage checkout smoke1 mybranch | sh
\&./elebake.sh stage make smoke1
\&./elebake.sh stage push smoke1 b
.Ed
.Pp
Migrate a database:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
env ELEBAKE_BASE=$HOME/.old/current ./elebake.sh dump > mig.sh
\&./elebake.sh bootstrap current minimal | sh
\&./elebake.sh restore mig.sh
.Ed
.Pp
Inspect instead of act
.Pq any command :
run it while the terminal default is
.Ql cat ,
read the emitted shell, then re-run under an executing pin.
